# uIOhook-napi Migration Guide

## Overview
The project has migrated from `iohook` to `uiohook-napi` for better Electron compatibility and modern Node.js support. This migration ensures compatibility with Node.js 18.18.2 + Electron 36.4.0.

## Key Implementation Files

### Core Hook Implementation
- [src/main/iohook.ts](mdc:src/main/iohook.ts) - Main uiohook-napi implementation
- [src/config/keys.ts](mdc:src/config/keys.ts) - Keycode mappings for iohook compatibility
- [src/config/settings.ts](mdc:src/config/settings.ts) - Type definitions and configuration
- [src/config/strings.ts](mdc:src/config/strings.ts) - String constants for logging

### Package Configuration
- [release/app/package.json](mdc:release/app/package.json) - Native dependency installation location
- [package.json](mdc:package.json) - Main package configuration (uiohook-napi should NOT be here)

## Migration Changes Made

### 1. Dependency Management
- ❌ Removed `iohook@^0.9.3` from main package.json
- ✅ Added `uiohook-napi@^1.5.4` to release/app/package.json (correct location for native deps)
- ✅ Removed iohook rebuild configuration

### 2. API Changes
```typescript
// OLD (iohook)
iohook.registerShortcut([trigger], onPress, onRelease);
iohook.on('mousedown', handler);
iohook.start();
iohook.unregisterAllShortcuts();

// NEW (uiohook-napi)
uIOhook.on('keydown', (event: UiohookKeyboardEvent) => { /* */ });
uIOhook.on('keyup', (event: UiohookKeyboardEvent) => { /* */ });
uIOhook.on('mousedown', (event: UiohookMouseEvent) => { /* */ });
uIOhook.start();
uIOhook.removeAllListeners('keydown');
```

### 3. Type System Updates
- `IOHookBehaviorType` → `UiohookBehaviorType`
- `IOHookInputType` → `UiohookInputType`
- Added proper TypeScript interfaces for events

## Installation Rules

### ✅ Correct Installation
```bash
cd release/app && npm install uiohook-napi@^1.5.4
```

### ❌ Incorrect Installation
```bash
npm install uiohook-napi  # Don't install in root package.json
```

## Usage Patterns

### Event Handling
- Use separate `keydown` and `keyup` listeners instead of registerShortcut
- Always type event parameters with proper interfaces
- Implement proper error handling with try-catch blocks

### State Management
- Use `isHookActive` boolean for tracking hook state
- Properly clean up listeners in stopIOHook function
- Handle errors gracefully during start/stop operations

## Compatibility
- ✅ Node.js 18.18.2
- ✅ Electron 36.4.0
- ✅ uiohook-napi 1.5.4
- ✅ Perfect compatibility for modern Electron apps
